00:17:25,208 --> 00:17:26,448
- So I can tell...
- The makeup that suits your image.

496
00:17:26,448 --> 00:17:28,548
- that she's an expert.
- Yes.

497
00:17:28,548 --> 00:17:31,488
I'm sure you get all kinds of clients here.

498
00:17:31,718 --> 00:17:34,488
You must've gotten a client that threw you off.

499
00:17:34,758 --> 00:17:37,388
I wouldn't say I was thrown off. But there were a few clients...

500
00:17:37,828 --> 00:17:40,258
I was determined to give my all for.

501
00:17:40,258 --> 00:17:42,858
- I felt this way only for...
- Yes.

502
00:17:42,998 --> 00:17:44,828
- two of my clients.
- Yes.

503
00:17:44,828 --> 00:17:48,298
They were going to the wedding of their ex-boyfriend.

504
00:17:48,368 --> 00:17:51,368
- What?
- They were attending the wedding.

505
00:17:51,738 --> 00:17:52,908
Both of them...

506
00:17:54,278 --> 00:17:55,338
As soon as they walked in, they said,

507
00:17:55,338 --> 00:17:58,608
"I'm so sorry to tell you this."

508
00:17:58,978 --> 00:18:01,578
"But I have to attend the wedding of my ex-boyfriend."

509
00:18:01,578 --> 00:18:03,148
- How did that happen?
- Right.

510
00:18:03,248 --> 00:18:05,748
Well, asking them what happened didn't feel right.

511
00:18:05,748 --> 00:18:07,058
- That's a sensitive topic.
- Yes.

512
00:18:07,688 --> 00:18:10,358
"Were you monkey branched? Did he ghost you?"

513
00:18:10,358 --> 00:18:12,558
"Just how bad of a jerk are we talking here?"

514
00:18:12,558 --> 00:18:15,358
I would ask questions along this line.

515
00:18:15,358 --> 00:18:17,528
- So the type of breakup...
- I'd ask these questions.

516
00:18:17,528 --> 00:18:19,568
- The intensity of the makeup...
- decides the intensity.

517
00:18:19,568 --> 00:18:21,738
I wanted to know how bad it was when they broke up.

518
00:18:21,738 --> 00:18:25,108
I'd ask if their new boyfriends were good enough to show off...

519
00:18:25,108 --> 00:18:26,938
or if they were going to the wedding with them.

520
00:18:26,938 --> 00:18:29,638
These were the questions I asked.

521
00:18:30,448 --> 00:18:32,408
I change the makeup based on the answers I get.

522
00:18:32,408 --> 00:18:33,778
I want to flip the question here.

523
00:18:33,778 --> 00:18:35,578
Let's say you get a new girlfriend.

524
00:18:35,578 --> 00:18:38,148
And if she asks you to go to her ex's wedding with her...

525
00:18:38,248 --> 00:18:39,688
- Should you go with her?
- The boyfriend...

526
00:18:40,288 --> 00:18:42,318
- If I were in his shoes...
- How should he dress up then?

527
00:18:42,318 --> 00:18:43,628
- For the wedding?
- If I were in his shoes,

528
00:18:43,928 --> 00:18:46,228
- I don't think I could go.
- He...

529
00:18:46,228 --> 00:18:49,628
He has to be completely decked out for the wedding.

530
00:18:49,898 --> 00:18:51,568
He's going there for her revenge.

531
00:18:51,568 --> 00:18:53,468
- To help her take revenge?
- Yes.

532
00:18:54,068 --> 00:18:56,098
- Should he go?
- The boyfriend...

533
00:18:56,098 --> 00:18:57,638
That's infuriating.

534
00:18:58,138 --> 00:18:59,708
Does it mean she's still hung up on the guy?

535
00:18:59,708 --> 00:19:01,378
What about me then? What does that say about me?

536
00:19:01,378 --> 00:19:02,638
She wouldn't share that much.

537
00:19:02,638 --> 00:19:03,908
- What do you think, guys?
- Well,

538
00:19:03,908 --> 00:19:05,008
like she explained,

539
00:19:05,008 --> 00:19:06,148
- if she must attend the wedding...
- Because they're colleagues.

540
00:19:06,148 --> 00:19:08,578
- because they're colleagues, - Right.

541
00:19:08,578 --> 00:19:09,848
I'd go all out after hearing the news.

542
00:19:10,018 --> 00:19:13,488
- Right.
- So she doesn't get hurt.

543
00:19:13,488 --> 00:19:14,618
That's what you'd do?

544
00:19:14,858 --> 00:19:16,988
- I'd dress up to the nines.
- That's it.

545
00:19:16,988 --> 00:19:18,828
- I'd look good effortlessly.
- That's what I thought.

546
00:19:18,828 --> 00:19:20,758
I'd come to this beauty salon.

547
00:19:20,758 --> 00:19:21,828
- They'd go together.
- At the end.

548
00:19:21,828 --> 00:19:22,958
What about you, Seung Ho?

549
00:19:22,958 --> 00:19:25,068
I don't know what the story is.

550
00:19:25,398 --> 00:19:27,068
But whatever it is, I don't think I can go.

551
00:19:27,068 --> 00:19:29,198
Exactly. You and I are on the same page.

552
00:19:29,638 --> 00:19:31,408
I don't think I can go.

553
00:19:31,408 --> 00:19:33,508
How could you let your girlfriend go by herself?

554
00:19:33,508 --> 00:19:35,078
The fact that she wants to go by herself...

555
00:19:35,078 --> 00:19:37,208
- I'd stop her.
- I need to stop her then.

556
00:19:37,208 --> 00:19:38,848
- That's understandable.
- "Don't go."

557
00:19:38,848 --> 00:19:41,378
- "Don't go to the wedding."
- "You don't have to attend it."

558
00:19:41,378 --> 00:19:42,648
- Exactly.
- But...

559
00:19:42,648 --> 00:19:45,088
if it's her colleague's wedding,

560
00:19:45,088 --> 00:19:46,348
and if only she doesn't attend it,

561
00:19:46,348 --> 00:19:48,488
- it would look weird.
- I'd understand it then.

562
00:19:48,758 --> 00:19:50,528
- If that's the case.
- She has no choice but to go.

563
00:19:50,528 --> 00:19:51,988
- She has no choice but to go.
- If she has no choice...

564
00:19:51,988 --> 00:19:53,528
- It seems we're on the same page.
- Right. No one...

565
00:19:53,528 --> 00:19:55,258
No one would want to go. But...

566
00:19:55,528 --> 00:19:58,098
- not attending the wedding...
- I'm sure she can give...

567
00:19:58,428 --> 00:19:59,528
- an explanation.
- That's possible too.

568
00:19:59,528 --> 00:20:01,538
If she's the only one who skips the wedding,

569
00:20:01,538 --> 00:20:04,138
it would be obvious that she skipped it because of him.

570
00:20:04,338 --> 00:20:06,008
Not to show that, she would have to go.

571
00:20:06,008 --> 00:20:07,138
- "I'm completely fine."
- But here's another possibility.

572
00:20:07,138 --> 00:20:08,678
It might sound like something far off in the future.

573
00:20:08,678 --> 00:20:11,008
But anything could happen between them in the future.

574
00:20:11,308 --> 00:20:12,948
Let's turn the tables around.

575
00:20:13,178 --> 00:20:14,948
Let's say I go to the wedding with her,

576
00:20:14,948 --> 00:20:16,348
so she gets her revenge.

577
00:20:16,348 --> 00:20:18,248
She's so happy, and I'm happy too.

578
00:20:18,518 --> 00:20:19,648
But then we break up...

579
00:20:19,858 --> 00:20:20,958
and I'm getting married.

580
00:20:21,118 --> 00:20:22,258
And she shows up...

581
00:20:23,058 --> 00:20:25,058
- She shows up at the wedding again?
- Why think that far ahead?

582
00:20:25,058 --> 00:20:26,698
Revenge begets revenge.

583
00:20:27,358 --> 00:20:28,858
Revenge begets revenge.

584
00:20:28,858 --> 00:20:30,768
Why can't you just dress up nicely...

585
00:20:30,768 --> 00:20:32,598
and go to the wedding for her sake?

586
00:20:32,598 --> 00:20:35,138
- I get your point. But...
- We're on the same page.

587
00:20:35,138 --> 00:20:36,338
- Yes.
- Gosh.

588
00:20:36,338 --> 00:20:39,168
- The ex-boyfriend...
- If they have no choice...

589
00:20:39,168 --> 00:20:41,308
but to attend the wedding, I'd understand.

590
00:20:41,608 --> 00:20:43,348
- But I wouldn't go if possible.
- Right.

591
00:20:43,348 --> 00:20:45,078
- I don't see any reason to go.
- Right.

592
00:20:45,078 --> 00:20:46,748
- I'd talk about that.
- I'd talk to her.

593
00:20:46,848 --> 00:20:48,848
- "You already won. You have me."
- You and I think alike. Yes.

594
00:20:48,848 --> 00:20:50,048
- Gosh, yes.
- So...

595
00:20:50,048 --> 00:20:51,848
- I'd try to cheer her up.
- You can afford to say that.

596
00:20:51,848 --> 00:20:52,948
Gosh, no.

597
00:20:53,488 --> 00:20:54,658
- I can't say that.
- No.

598
00:20:55,118 --> 00:20:57,028
If he were my boyfriend, I wouldn't go.

599
00:20:57,328 --> 00:20:59,158
- I wouldn't go then.
- I wouldn't go either.

600
00:20:59,158 --> 00:21:01,398
(He ends the heated debate.)

601
00:21:01,398 --> 00:21:03,228
All right. Let's spice up her day...

602
00:21:03,428 --> 00:21:05,298
- with a little excitement.
- Yes.

603
00:21:05,298 --> 00:21:07,298
Young Hyun and Seung Ho are here.

604
00:21:07,298 --> 00:21:09,498
If we make it to Round Three, we're going to Wolfgang's.

605
00:21:10,768 --> 00:21:12,268
- You will?
- Yes, we will.

606
00:21:12,938 --> 00:21:14,478
Let's go to Wolfgang's Steakhouse if we make it to Round Three.

607
00:21:14,478 --> 00:21:16,238
- Let's do it.
- Yes, let's do it.

608
00:21:16,778 --> 00:21:18,908
- Let me open this up.
- Okay.

609
00:21:19,278 --> 00:21:20,578
- I'm excited.
- Yes.

610
00:21:20,848 --> 00:21:21,978
"I've been running for two weeks."

611
00:21:21,978 --> 00:21:24,418
"It will be a great workout partner for a novice runner."

612
00:21:24,418 --> 00:21:26,088
"A Garmin smartwatch."

613
00:21:27,018 --> 00:21:28,258
"A smartwatch."

614
00:21:28,418 --> 00:21:30,788
(The essential item for runners, Garmin smartwatch)

615
00:21:31,088 --> 00:21:32,558
(A must-have for avid runners)

616
00:21:32,558 --> 00:21:35,928
Did you pick up running lately?

617
00:21:36,158 --> 00:21:38,528
- I picked up running as my hobby.
- Yes.

618
00:21:38,698 --> 00:21:40,698
I'm not in any running crew.

619
00:21:40,698 --> 00:21:43,168
- Have you heard of covert running?
- What's that?

620
00:21:43,308 --> 00:21:44,538
Let's say I go out for a run.

621
00:21:44,708 --> 00:21:47,178
- And you're on your run too.
- Yes.

622
00:21:47,178 --> 00:21:49,678
I would run up behind you and secretly tag along.

623
00:21:51,008 --> 00:21:53,618
- Then I'd run behind him.
- To set your pace to his pace?

624
00:21:53,618 --> 00:21:55,318
Yes. I would do that. So let's say I'm running behind him.

625
00:21:55,448 --> 00:21:58,588
When Young K senses something and turns around to look,

626
00:21:58,748 --> 00:22:00,058
- I'd run away.
- Do you go somewhere else?

627
00:22:00,388 --> 00:22:02,618
Afterward, I'd keep running.

628
00:22:02,918 --> 00:22:05,288
When I spot Yeon Seok running, I'd stay with him then.

629
00:22:05,288 --> 00:22:06,558
I'd keep running behind him.

630
00:22:06,558 --> 00:22:08,098
When he senses my presence and turns around,

631
00:22:08,098 --> 00:22:09,528
I'd run away again.

632
00:22:09,528 --> 00:22:10,868
- That's covert running.
- Mi Ri.

633
00:22:10,998 --> 00:22:13,868
- You do all kinds of activities.
- Why is she doing that?

634
00:22:14,338 --> 00:22:16,838
- She does all kinds of things.
- I've been on covert running.

635
00:22:16,838 --> 00:22:18,168
- I don't have...
- Do you need this watch?

636
00:22:18,168 --> 00:22:19,908
a workout buddy.

637
00:22:20,178 --> 00:22:21,578
You don't know how to go about this...

638
00:22:21,578 --> 00:22:22,978
- when you're on your own.
- Right.

639
00:22:23,108 --> 00:22:25,308
- But I don't get in their way.
- You make sure of that.

640
00:22:25,308 --> 00:22:27,018
I secretly set my pace to other people's.

641
00:22:27,018 --> 00:22:30,048
- This can help you keep your pace.
- I've never heard of this.

642
00:22:30,048 --> 00:22:32,188
- Of course.
- We need to win this for you.

643
00:22:32,318 --> 00:22:33,658
- Thank you.
- She's so funny.

644
00:22:33,658 --> 00:22:36,288
- She's funny.
- I'm grateful for this.

645
00:22:36,458 --> 00:22:37,458
Okay.

646
00:22:37,458 --> 00:22:38,858
(One Shot! Closing)

647
00:22:38,858 --> 00:22:40,058
(Finger flick the bottle cap...)

648
00:22:40,058 --> 00:22:42,758
(and close the lid of a cosmetic product.)

649
00:22:42,758 --> 00:22:46,968
(Round 1: 2 eyeshadow palettes)

650
00:22:46,968 --> 00:22:48,598
(They're given 10 bottle caps.)

651
00:22:48,598 --> 00:22:50,738
(But they only have 30 seconds.)

652
00:22:52,038 --> 00:22:54,378
(It's like Alkkagi.)

653
00:22:54,538 --> 00:22:55,708
Gosh, what's this now?

654
00:22:56,108 --> 00:22:57,578
In the end, it's all about finger flicks.

655
00:22:57,578 --> 00:22:59,408
We need to close it with the bottle caps.

656
00:23:00,548 --> 00:23:02,348
They want us to close the lid.

657
00:23:03,348 --> 00:23:05,618
I think we need to hit it pretty hard.

658
00:23:05,618 --> 00:23:07,158
- Exactly. This game...
- This is...

659
00:23:09,058 --> 00:23:11,258
- I'm not wearing a thimble.
- That was too strong.

660
00:23:13,328 --> 00:23:14,858
That was too strong as well. Hold on.

661
00:23:16,328 --> 00:23:17,528
