00:42:49,941 --> 00:42:52,151
- I'm now older than them.
- Exactly.

1246
00:42:52,151 --> 00:42:53,611
- They speak formally to you.
- Yes.

1247
00:42:53,611 --> 00:42:55,211
- That's right.
- They treat me like an old veteran.

1248
00:42:55,211 --> 00:42:56,321
(Nowadays, they treat him like a veteran actor.)

1249
00:42:56,321 --> 00:42:58,921
You made your debut a long time ago,

1250
00:42:58,921 --> 00:43:01,121
- so you're a veteran actor.
- He's a veteran actor.

1251
00:43:01,121 --> 00:43:02,791
- Exactly.
- When did you make your debut?

1252
00:43:03,221 --> 00:43:05,661
- I started working in 1998.
- Goodness.

1253
00:43:06,691 --> 00:43:08,131
He's more experienced than I am.

1254
00:43:08,131 --> 00:43:09,301
(Unbelievable years of experience)

1255
00:43:09,961 --> 00:43:12,301
(Whopping 29 years of experience!)

1256
00:43:12,301 --> 00:43:13,331
- That's crazy.
- I know.

1257
00:43:13,331 --> 00:43:14,971
I made my debut in 2003.

1258
00:43:15,301 --> 00:43:16,741
- Really?
- Really?

1259
00:43:16,741 --> 00:43:18,571
- Yes.
- He has more experience than you.

1260
00:43:20,341 --> 00:43:22,211
I was a clueless baby back then.

1261
00:43:22,981 --> 00:43:25,351
You don't remember everything in those years, do you?

1262
00:43:25,351 --> 00:43:26,511
Like the works.

1263
00:43:27,251 --> 00:43:28,881
- I can't remember everything.
- Exactly.

1264
00:43:28,881 --> 00:43:30,981
But I remember the ones...

1265
00:43:30,981 --> 00:43:33,151
- that left huge impressions.
- I see.

1266
00:43:33,151 --> 00:43:34,951
As you know, the atmosphere on set was...

1267
00:43:35,461 --> 00:43:36,661
- tough back then.
- Yes.

1268
00:43:36,791 --> 00:43:38,191
- It was very... Yes.
- It was the age of savagery.

1269
00:43:38,191 --> 00:43:39,291
Savagery...

1270
00:43:39,291 --> 00:43:40,661
It was the age of savagery.

1271
00:43:40,761 --> 00:43:42,161
It was so brutal.

1272
00:43:42,401 --> 00:43:43,531
They stayed up all nights...

1273
00:43:43,531 --> 00:43:45,471
and went through so much to film.

1274
00:43:45,471 --> 00:43:47,371
That's right. They didn't have that before.

1275
00:43:47,371 --> 00:43:49,371
Now, a child actor can work until certain hours.

1276
00:43:49,371 --> 00:43:50,371
- You're right.
- That's the law.

1277
00:43:50,371 --> 00:43:51,371
You have to send them home before midnight.

1278
00:43:51,371 --> 00:43:54,211
They let child actors go home before 10pm.

1279
00:43:54,211 --> 00:43:56,011
The shooting environment has gotten much better now.

1280
00:43:56,011 --> 00:43:57,481
- Yes.
- That's right.

1281
00:43:57,981 --> 00:43:59,951
When I shot for "Flex x Cop 2,"

1282
00:44:00,111 --> 00:44:02,981
it was my first time working in the environment...

1283
00:44:02,981 --> 00:44:04,881
that had changed in a good way.

1284
00:44:05,081 --> 00:44:06,991
When I shot dramas in the past,

1285
00:44:07,221 --> 00:44:09,221
- I used to stay up three nights.
- Yes.

1286
00:44:09,221 --> 00:44:10,391
So, I thought it'd be easy.

1287
00:44:10,891 --> 00:44:12,161
But I got exhausted...

1288
00:44:12,831 --> 00:44:14,091
after the shootings.

1289
00:44:14,631 --> 00:44:16,261
They finished shooting on time,

1290
00:44:16,261 --> 00:44:17,561
but I passed out after it.

1291
00:44:17,561 --> 00:44:19,031
- Because it's been a while.
- Yes.

1292
00:44:19,171 --> 00:44:21,471
People change. You get used to it quickly.

1293
00:44:21,471 --> 00:44:22,941
- That's how it is.
- Yes.

1294
00:44:23,301 --> 00:44:24,441
- Your food is here.
- Okay.

1295
00:44:24,441 --> 00:44:25,741
- Thank you.
- Okay. Thank you.

1296
00:44:25,741 --> 00:44:26,811
Here.

1297
00:44:27,571 --> 00:44:30,381
- Gosh. It's been a while.
- Yes. It was just like this.

1298
00:44:31,011 --> 00:44:32,781
- That's right.
- Goodness.

1299
00:44:33,781 --> 00:44:35,211
They served us a trayful of dishes.

1300
00:44:35,751 --> 00:44:38,551
Goodness. This is how they serve.

1301
00:44:39,091 --> 00:44:40,621
Gosh. They look good.

1302
00:44:40,791 --> 00:44:42,021
- They look tasty, right?
- Yes.

1303
00:44:42,691 --> 00:44:43,861
Gosh. Look.

1304
00:44:43,861 --> 00:44:45,221
It looks so good.

1305
00:44:45,221 --> 00:44:47,091
- It's been a while.
- This is it.

1306
00:44:47,091 --> 00:44:48,701
- This is it.
- This really is it.

1307
00:44:49,261 --> 00:44:51,361
- I'm glad we came here.
- Yes. It's been a while.

1308
00:44:51,901 --> 00:44:53,331
It has been so long.

1309
00:44:53,331 --> 00:44:55,101
Steak must've been good too, though.

1310
00:44:55,101 --> 00:44:56,701
(The taste of the past that is as precious as or more than steak)

1311
00:44:56,701 --> 00:44:58,471
- Thanks for the food.
- Please enjoy.

1312
00:44:58,471 --> 00:44:59,871
- Enjoy.
- Thanks for the food.

1313
00:44:59,871 --> 00:45:01,211
- The stew...
- We don't know who'll pay.

1314
00:45:01,211 --> 00:45:02,581
Let's just dig in for now.

1315
00:45:02,641 --> 00:45:04,081
- The table will collapse.
- You brought your cards, right?

1316
00:45:04,081 --> 00:45:06,151
- Yes, I brought it.
- I brought it.

1317
00:45:07,011 --> 00:45:08,981
- Here, Seung Ho.
- Okay. Thanks.

1318
00:45:09,651 --> 00:45:11,921
This is just perfect on a rainy day.

1319
00:45:12,221 --> 00:45:13,291
Gosh. Thank you.

1320
00:45:16,021 --> 00:45:17,191
The side dishes are so tasty.

1321
00:45:17,191 --> 00:45:18,191
(Satisfied)

1322
00:45:18,731 --> 00:45:21,731
(Taking a bite of good old memories)

1323
00:45:21,731 --> 00:45:22,801
Gosh. Hey.

1324
00:45:22,801 --> 00:45:24,001
It still tastes great.

1325
00:45:24,001 --> 00:45:25,201
- Yes.
- Gosh.

1326
00:45:25,201 --> 00:45:26,901
It tastes like I remember it.

1327
00:45:30,401 --> 00:45:31,741
I came here after an audition...

1328
00:45:32,641 --> 00:45:34,841
