1329
00:45:35,581 --> 00:45:37,581
"Hey, let's just eat for now."

1330
00:45:38,141 --> 00:45:39,651
- This is the taste of rookie years.
- Yes.

1331
00:45:40,011 --> 00:45:42,011
Yeon Shik had these during his rookie season.

1332
00:45:43,421 --> 00:45:44,521
It's tasty.

1333
00:45:45,021 --> 00:45:46,221
You're eating well, Seung Ho.

1334
00:45:47,321 --> 00:45:48,421
It's so good.

1335
00:45:48,721 --> 00:45:50,791
What's your family like? Do you have siblings?

1336
00:45:51,161 --> 00:45:53,691
I'm an only child.

1337
00:45:54,431 --> 00:45:55,931
I lived away from my parents since I graduated...

1338
00:45:55,931 --> 00:45:57,431
from elementary school.

1339
00:45:57,631 --> 00:45:58,801
I went to study abroad alone.

1340
00:45:59,471 --> 00:46:02,241
When I came back to be a trainee at JYP Entertainment,

1341
00:46:02,441 --> 00:46:03,871
they no longer needed to look after me.

1342
00:46:03,871 --> 00:46:05,171
They left for Canada instead.

1343
00:46:05,171 --> 00:46:06,441
(After he became a trainee, they moved to Canada.)

1344
00:46:06,441 --> 00:46:08,911
- We switched places.
- I see.

1345
00:46:09,141 --> 00:46:10,441
- Gosh.
- They're in Canada.

1346
00:46:10,441 --> 00:46:11,911
- Yes.
- You're amazing, Young Hyun.

1347
00:46:12,651 --> 00:46:14,081
- It's not easy to live alone.
- I've been enjoying my life.

1348
00:46:14,211 --> 00:46:15,451
I can't do it.

1349
00:46:16,081 --> 00:46:18,521
The English you learned back then...

1350
00:46:18,621 --> 00:46:20,621
must be so useful in your singing career.

1351
00:46:20,821 --> 00:46:23,291
I'm so glad about it because...

1352
00:46:23,721 --> 00:46:25,291
it's easier for me when I work.

1353
00:46:25,831 --> 00:46:27,931
- That's right.
- When I was in college,

1354
00:46:27,931 --> 00:46:30,631
my major was taught mainly in English.

1355
00:46:30,831 --> 00:46:32,331
So it helped me a lot.

1356
00:46:32,501 --> 00:46:34,671
- And I served as KATUSA.
- That's right.

1357
00:46:35,271 --> 00:46:37,501
In fact, as for DAY6,

1358
00:46:38,441 --> 00:46:40,171
it wasn't exactly...

1359
00:46:40,371 --> 00:46:42,681
- super well-known...
- Right.

1360
00:46:42,981 --> 00:46:45,081
- group.
- That's right.

1361
00:46:45,811 --> 00:46:49,181
But the old songs made it back into the charts all together.

1362
00:46:49,621 --> 00:46:51,851
Gosh. What a life.

1363
00:46:52,751 --> 00:46:55,391
- It's amazing.
- How many years...

1364
00:46:55,391 --> 00:46:57,691
did you spend as a lesser-known group?

1365
00:46:58,831 --> 00:47:02,261
"You Were Beautiful" made it back into the charts after six years...

1366
00:47:02,261 --> 00:47:04,631
- Exactly.
- since its release.

1367
00:47:04,901 --> 00:47:07,371
Because you have great songs...

1368
00:47:07,371 --> 00:47:09,301
and talents to support them,

1369
00:47:09,941 --> 00:47:12,041
when people recognized you,

1370
00:47:12,441 --> 00:47:14,271
- it created a synergy.
- They were ready.

1371
00:47:15,271 --> 00:47:17,411
- There aren't many 24-hour spots.
- Not anymore.

1372
00:47:17,411 --> 00:47:19,711
- They used to fill Gangnam.
- There were many.

1373
00:47:20,481 --> 00:47:22,521
It's because labor costs have skyrocketed.

1374
00:47:22,681 --> 00:47:23,781
Now...

1375
00:47:23,921 --> 00:47:25,021
- Eat comfortably.
- I'll eat some more.

1376
00:47:25,421 --> 00:47:26,591
Do you want more rice?

1377
00:47:26,591 --> 00:47:28,021
It's okay. This will be enough.

1378
00:47:29,261 --> 00:47:31,561
(The big eater is still hungry.)

1379
00:47:33,261 --> 00:47:34,631
(Satisfied)

1380
00:47:35,461 --> 00:47:37,101
(Taking another spoonful)

1381
00:47:37,101 --> 00:47:39,801
They all look at their phones while working on set.

1382
00:47:39,801 --> 00:47:42,701
(Eating with passion while even sweating)

1383
00:47:43,341 --> 00:47:44,941
(Taking another spoonful)

1384
00:47:44,941 --> 00:47:46,271
I really enjoyed it.

1385
00:47:46,271 --> 00:47:47,371
Order more.

1386
00:47:47,511 --> 00:47:49,081
It's good.

1387
00:47:49,081 --> 00:47:50,441
- This nurungji is good.
- Nurungji is good, right?

1388
00:47:50,441 --> 00:47:52,111
- It's good.
- Their nurungji is...

1389
00:47:52,111 --> 00:47:54,011
- I think I ate half of it.
- Their nurungji is...

1390
00:47:54,011 --> 00:47:55,881
No. You can have more.

1391
00:47:57,021 --> 00:47:59,651
- It's flavorful.
- Yes. It's aromatic.

1392
00:48:00,391 --> 00:48:01,551
(They're done with the satisfying lunch.)

1393
00:48:01,551 --> 00:48:02,761
- Gosh.
- That's right.

1394
00:48:02,821 --> 00:48:05,791
- Now, we need to pay.
- Yes. We need to play a game.

1395
00:48:06,031 --> 00:48:07,791
Is there a game you play with your friends?

1396
00:48:07,791 --> 00:48:09,331
- Any games?
- Well...

1397
00:48:09,701 --> 00:48:11,561
We play a ghost leg.

1398
00:48:11,561 --> 00:48:13,131
- A ghost leg.
- We play that.

1399
00:48:13,271 --> 00:48:14,731
- Let's go classic this time.
- Okay.

1400
00:48:14,731 --> 00:48:15,801
- Yes.
- The numbers...

1401
00:48:15,801 --> 00:48:17,801
It's been a really long time since I actually drew one.

1402
00:48:17,801 --> 00:48:19,441
- That's right.
- We're going analog.

1403
00:48:19,441 --> 00:48:21,811
Okay. I added more steps because it was empty.

1404
00:48:22,111 --> 00:48:23,781
- You have to add more at the end.
- You can't calculate the result.

1405
00:48:24,341 --> 00:48:25,441
Draw them comfortably.

1406
00:48:25,711 --> 00:48:26,751
It has to go like this.

1407
00:48:26,751 --> 00:48:27,911
In the end.

1408
00:48:27,911 --> 00:48:29,351
(Adding the final twist)

1409
00:48:30,781 --> 00:48:32,421
How many are you drawing?

1410
00:48:33,391 --> 00:48:34,751
- I gave it lots of twists.
- Now.

1411
00:48:35,761 --> 00:48:38,291
- Which one should we start with?
- Let's go with number one.

1412
00:48:38,421 --> 00:48:39,591
- Number one?
- Yes.

1413
00:48:39,791 --> 00:48:41,361
- Young K?
- Yes. I'll sing.

1414
00:48:46,131 --> 00:48:47,331
If number one gets it, the game is over.

1415
00:48:47,871 --> 00:48:48,901
- What?
- What?

1416
00:48:50,541 --> 00:48:51,741
Wait. It goes this way, right?

1417
00:48:53,541 --> 00:48:55,071
- Yes!
- Gosh.

1418
00:48:55,711 --> 00:48:57,281
Yes!

1419
00:48:57,641 --> 00:48:58,841
Good job, Seung Ho.

1420
00:49:00,381 --> 00:49:01,881
If you didn't add the line, I had to pay.

1421
00:49:01,881 --> 00:49:03,121
- It was good, wasn't it?
- Yes.

1422
00:49:03,421 --> 00:49:05,021
- Should we go in order?
- Sounds good.

1423
00:49:05,021 --> 00:49:07,491
- Okay. Let's go.
- Number two is Seung Ho.

1424
00:49:07,791 --> 00:49:08,891
