1519
00:52:28,051 --> 00:52:29,761
Seung Ho has worked in the entertainment business...

1520
00:52:29,761 --> 00:52:31,461
for quite some time,

1521
00:52:31,461 --> 00:52:32,691
- so he's not to be underestimated.
- You're right.

1522
00:52:33,561 --> 00:52:35,331
You're good. You have to be tough.

1523
00:52:35,331 --> 00:52:36,361
(Getting ready to order more)

1524
00:52:36,361 --> 00:52:38,231
- You have to be tough, Seung Ho.
- Okay.

1525
00:52:38,631 --> 00:52:40,571
- A red bean brownie and...
- A red bean brownie.

1526
00:52:40,771 --> 00:52:42,331
- And..
- And a carrot cake.

1527
00:52:42,331 --> 00:52:44,571
Milk bingsu must be nice and fluffy.

1528
00:52:44,971 --> 00:52:46,641
You should order it since you're paying for it.

1529
00:52:46,841 --> 00:52:48,071
(Another dish was added.)

1530
00:52:48,071 --> 00:52:50,081
- You're a veteran actor.
- Sir.

1531
00:52:50,211 --> 00:52:51,711
- Sir.
- Thank you, sir.

1532
00:52:51,711 --> 00:52:53,181
Please order those two, sir.

1533
00:52:53,181 --> 00:52:55,011
- Okay.
- A milk bingsu for one person.

1534
00:52:55,011 --> 00:52:56,221
Okay.

1535
00:52:57,581 --> 00:52:58,681
Okay.

1536
00:52:59,351 --> 00:53:00,351
Thank you.

1537
00:53:00,351 --> 00:53:01,721
Okay. Thank you.

1538
00:53:02,151 --> 00:53:04,561
- You ordered one more milk bingsu?
- Yes, I did.

1539
00:53:05,791 --> 00:53:07,461
Milk bingsu does sound good.

1540
00:53:07,731 --> 00:53:09,761
That one doesn't come with red beans.

1541
00:53:09,761 --> 00:53:10,901
You're right.

1542
00:53:10,901 --> 00:53:13,471
It's perfect if you're on a diet.

1543
00:53:13,601 --> 00:53:14,601
Which one?

1544
00:53:14,771 --> 00:53:15,771
The milk bingsu.

1545
00:53:15,771 --> 00:53:17,441
Did you say milk bingsu is weight-loss-friendly?

1546
00:53:17,641 --> 00:53:19,241
It seems low-calorie.

1547
00:53:19,611 --> 00:53:22,171
- They use organic sugar.
- Yes. They use organic sugar too.

1548
00:53:22,641 --> 00:53:24,311
Gosh. JYP Entertainment is all about organic food.

1549
00:53:24,741 --> 00:53:25,781
For real.

1550
00:53:27,081 --> 00:53:29,321
They love organic stuff.

1551
00:53:29,321 --> 00:53:31,321
It must be great. For lunch,

1552
00:53:31,321 --> 00:53:33,421
- They have organic menus.
- they serve organic food.

1553
00:53:33,621 --> 00:53:35,621
- Now...
- They used to be in Cheongdam.

1554
00:53:35,621 --> 00:53:36,821
- The small building.
- The small one.

1555
00:53:37,061 --> 00:53:38,121
- I'm from that building.
- Right.

1556
00:53:38,121 --> 00:53:39,731
Since it was in that building? That's a long time.

1557
00:53:39,731 --> 00:53:40,861
We're divided.

1558
00:53:40,991 --> 00:53:42,731
Those who were trainees at the old building.

1559
00:53:43,161 --> 00:53:45,731
Those who were trainees at the training center...

1560
00:53:45,971 --> 00:53:47,871
which was in a separate building...

1561
00:53:47,871 --> 00:53:49,841
- next to a movie theater.
- That's right. Right next to it.

1562
00:53:50,441 --> 00:53:51,701
Those who trained there.

1563
00:53:52,341 --> 00:53:53,541
And those who trained...

1564
00:53:53,541 --> 00:53:54,771
- in the new building.
- I see.

1565
00:53:54,771 --> 00:53:56,411
We're divided into those generations.

1566
00:53:56,711 --> 00:53:57,881
Our group is from Cheongdam.

1567
00:53:57,881 --> 00:53:59,141
(They're the 1st generation, trained in Cheongdam.)

1568
00:53:59,581 --> 00:54:00,981
- Yes.
- You paid for several pillars...

1569
00:54:00,981 --> 00:54:02,351
at the new building.

1570
00:54:02,511 --> 00:54:04,451
Maybe several windows.

1571
00:54:04,451 --> 00:54:06,451
- Window frames?
- Yes.

1572
00:54:06,791 --> 00:54:10,261
It's because there are great singers who came before us.

1573
00:54:10,261 --> 00:54:12,691
Still, the window frames on that building...

1574
00:54:12,861 --> 00:54:14,661
- are quite expensive.
- First of all,

1575
00:54:14,891 --> 00:54:16,631
- there's TWICE.
- TWICE.

1576
00:54:17,361 --> 00:54:18,901
They paid for the structure.

1577
00:54:18,901 --> 00:54:22,201
They do tours in stadiums.

1578
00:54:22,371 --> 00:54:23,841
Jin Young and I are...

1579
00:54:23,841 --> 00:54:25,071
- Gosh.
- Goodness.

1580
00:54:26,271 --> 00:54:27,311
Their red beans are different.

1581
00:54:27,511 --> 00:54:29,581
- Gosh. Thank you.
- Thank you.

1582
00:54:29,581 --> 00:54:30,711
- Thank you for the food.
- Thank you.

1583
00:54:30,711 --> 00:54:33,251
- Thank you, Seung Ho.
- Yes, thank you.

1584
00:54:33,551 --> 00:54:35,211
She boiled the red beans herself.

1585
00:54:35,211 --> 00:54:37,151
(Red bean paste made from scratch)

1586
00:54:37,221 --> 00:54:38,751
- Gosh.
- We can have it as is.

1587
00:54:38,751 --> 00:54:41,651
(The highly anticipated first bite)

1588
00:54:43,321 --> 00:54:45,061
- Gosh. It's good.
- It's really good.

1589
00:54:45,061 --> 00:54:46,631
- It's soft.
- Yes.

1590
00:54:47,091 --> 00:54:50,101
These red beans are not too strong.

1591
00:54:50,231 --> 00:54:51,231
- Really?
- Yes.

1592
00:54:51,731 --> 00:54:52,731
(The spoons come together.)

1593
00:54:52,731 --> 00:54:54,371
- It's good.
- It's delicious, ma'am.

1594
00:54:54,371 --> 00:54:55,401
Ma'am.

1595
00:54:55,571 --> 00:54:56,641
(Young K's big eater mode is on.)

1596
00:54:56,641 --> 00:54:58,501
It's so tasty. It's milk bingsu too.

1597
00:54:58,501 --> 00:54:59,941
- People will line up now.
- It's amazing, ma'am.

1598
00:54:59,941 --> 00:55:01,441
(Devouring it as if they haven't eaten for days)

1599
00:55:01,441 --> 00:55:02,541
It's really good.

1600
00:55:02,941 --> 00:55:04,341
The rice cake on top of it is really good.

1601
00:55:04,341 --> 00:55:05,781
I just had one too.

1602
00:55:06,581 --> 00:55:07,611
It's really good.

1603
00:55:07,611 --> 00:55:09,321
(They can't stop eating it.)

1604
00:55:09,321 --> 00:55:10,551
This is worth the drive.

1605
00:55:11,481 --> 00:55:12,921
Gosh. We finished it.

1606
00:55:13,221 --> 00:55:14,251
It's gone.

1607
00:55:14,451 --> 00:55:16,991
It's been so long since I finished a whole bingsu.

1608
00:55:17,091 --> 00:55:19,161
- Gosh. It's good.
- Really.

1609
00:55:19,661 --> 00:55:20,891
Nice. The cab is booked.

1610
00:55:20,891 --> 00:55:21,931
(Navi Yoo called a cab in time.)

1611
00:55:22,091 --> 00:55:24,261
(But he can't let go of his spoon.)

1612
00:55:24,261 --> 00:55:25,831
- Gosh. Ma'am.
- We finished them.

1613
00:55:25,961 --> 00:55:28,531
You're eating it as if you're eating gukbap.

1614
00:55:29,001 --> 00:55:30,441
Gosh. He's...

1615
00:55:30,871 --> 00:55:33,511
- Gosh. You're really eating it.
- You're eating bingsu...

1616
00:55:34,141 --> 00:55:35,771
- like gukbap.
- He must love it.

1617
00:55:36,341 --> 00:55:37,341
(Let's go.)

1618
00:55:37,341 --> 00:55:39,481
- It's here.
- Let's go. It's here.

1619
00:55:40,351 --> 00:55:42,251
- We loved it, ma'am.
- We enjoyed it so much.

1620
00:55:42,251 --> 00:55:43,321
It was really good.

1621
00:55:43,321 --> 00:55:45,081
- Thank you.
- Bye.

1622
00:55:45,381 --> 00:55:46,791
- Gosh. That was good.
- That was great.

1623
00:55:46,791 --> 00:55:48,391
Today's lunch was amazing.

1624
00:55:48,391 --> 00:55:50,061
- Seriously.
- That bingsu.

1625
00:55:50,061 --> 00:55:52,291
Gosh. You had it as if it were a hangover soup.

1626
00:55:53,031 --> 00:55:54,491
It was totally my kind of bingsu.

1627
00:55:54,491 --> 00:55:55,761
- You had bingsu as if it were soup.
- I've never seen anyone...

1628
00:55:55,761 --> 00:55:57,031
eating it like that.

1629
00:55:57,201 --> 00:55:59,671
Maybe I ate too much of your nurungji.

1630
00:56:01,101 --> 00:56:03,071
- No, I had my portion of nurungji.
- You needed more food.

1631
00:56:03,071 --> 00:56:04,141
No.

1632
00:56:04,641 --> 00:56:06,041
You actually don't go around...

1633
00:56:06,341 --> 00:56:08,911
in a car booked for the shoot.

1634
00:56:08,911 --> 00:56:09,941
- No.
- I called the cab.

1635
00:56:09,941 --> 00:56:10,981
Exactly.

1636
00:56:10,981 --> 00:56:12,481
- I have to call them.
- Most of the taxi fares...

1637
00:56:12,811 --> 00:56:14,111
are on him.

1638
00:56:14,111 --> 00:56:15,251
I pay for the cabs.

1639
00:56:15,911 --> 00:56:18,921
And if I pay for the lunch too...

1640
00:56:18,921 --> 00:56:20,521
Right. You're on point.

1641
00:56:20,721 --> 00:56:22,021
I can understand you now.

1642
00:56:22,391 --> 00:56:24,191
Now, for this last one,

1643
00:56:25,391 --> 00:56:26,531
let's do our best.

1644
00:56:26,961 --> 00:56:28,691
I feel pressure.

1645
00:56:28,691 --> 00:56:29,701
(Intimidated)

1646
00:56:29,901 --> 00:56:31,631
It's because I didn't pay for lunch...

1647
00:56:32,061 --> 00:56:33,231
or desserts.

1648
00:56:33,801 --> 00:56:34,871
I never paid.

1649
00:56:35,431 --> 00:56:37,871
- You excelled at not paying.
- Right.

1650
00:56:38,001 --> 00:56:39,711
- I should do my part now.
- You're lucky.

1651
00:56:40,541 --> 00:56:41,871
I wonder what game we'll play.

1652
00:56:43,081 --> 00:56:44,781
- "Lee Ye Won."
- Ye Won.

1653
00:56:44,781 --> 00:56:47,551
"I'm curious about a day of our diligent princess..."

1654
00:56:47,551 --> 00:56:49,581
"who goes to work every day.."

1655
00:56:49,581 --> 00:56:51,551
- "through the morning dew."
- What?

1656
00:56:51,821 --> 00:56:53,721
"It's fluffy and sweet."

1657
00:56:54,151 --> 00:56:56,861
"It's puffy and round. We love it."

1658
00:56:56,861 --> 00:56:58,161
Is it a children's song?

1659
00:56:58,821 --> 00:57:00,561
"My daughter spends all day..."

1660
00:57:00,561 --> 00:57:02,931
"basking in the glow of dreams, not the sun."

1661
00:57:02,931 --> 00:57:04,801
"Please go see her on my behalf."

1662
00:57:04,801 --> 00:57:07,331
Is her daughter an employee who's working at a certain place?

1663
00:57:07,771 --> 00:57:10,471
She spends all day basking in the glow of dreams, not the sun.

1664
00:57:10,471 --> 00:57:12,541
- Is she a student?
- Exactly.

1665
00:57:12,541 --> 00:57:13,941
That might be right.

1666
00:57:13,971 --> 00:57:16,111
- Her mother sent the letter, right?
- Yes.

1667
00:57:16,381 --> 00:57:17,841
Round and...

1668
00:57:18,081 --> 00:57:19,851
- There was a song.
- "It's puffy..."

1669
00:57:19,851 --> 00:57:21,251
"and round. We love it."

1670
00:57:21,811 --> 00:57:23,251
"It's fluffy and sweet."

1671
00:57:23,851 --> 00:57:25,621
It's puffy and round?

1672
00:57:25,621 --> 00:57:27,621
- Cotton candy?
- Does she make those?

1673
00:57:27,791 --> 00:57:29,891
- Sticky rice cake?
- I can only think of food.

1674
00:57:29,891 --> 00:57:31,091
I have no idea.

1675
00:57:31,791 --> 00:57:32,891
What?

1676
00:57:33,191 --> 00:57:34,791
It's Grand InterContinental...

1677
00:57:34,791 --> 00:57:36,631
- It's at Parnas.
- It's Parnas.

1678
00:57:36,931 --> 00:57:38,001
Is it at a hotel?

1679
00:57:38,461 --> 00:57:39,931
What is she doing at a hotel?

1680
00:57:41,131 --> 00:57:42,531
Hold on. Where did you say it was?

1681
00:57:42,531 --> 00:57:43,601
(Where is Whenever Guest in the 5-star hotel?)

1682
00:57:43,901 --> 00:57:47,111
She told us to find the white hat around here.

1683
00:57:48,471 --> 00:57:49,981
What? Where is this place?

1684
00:57:50,511 --> 00:57:51,941
I think it's near there.

1685
00:57:51,941 --> 00:57:53,581
- Wait. They're wearing a hat.
- Right.

1686
00:57:53,751 --> 00:57:55,481
- They must be pastry chefs.
- There they are.

1687
00:57:55,481 --> 00:57:56,821
- Is she the one?
- Yes, pastry chefs.

1688
00:57:57,081 --> 00:57:58,521
Gosh. They're here. It's crazy.

1689
00:57:59,051 --> 00:58:00,491
- What?
- He's so handsome.

1690
00:58:00,491 --> 00:58:01,951
- Who?
- Yeon Seok's really hot.

1691
00:58:01,951 --> 00:58:03,261
(Those in white hats are responding transparently.)

1692
00:58:03,261 --> 00:58:05,191
They're staring at us. We should pretend to hang around.

1693
00:58:05,521 --> 00:58:06,631
- Ye Won?
- Ye Won.

1694
00:58:06,631 --> 00:58:08,161
- Who's Ye Won?
- Gosh.

1695
00:58:08,161 --> 00:58:09,291
Hello.

1696
00:58:09,291 --> 00:58:11,131
- Hello.
- Nice to meet you.

1697
00:58:12,161 --> 00:58:13,571
Right. You're wearing name tags.

1698
00:58:14,101 --> 00:58:15,701
- Ye Won?
- Yes.

1699
00:58:15,931 --> 00:58:17,471
Hello. Nice to meet you.

1700
00:58:17,601 --> 00:58:19,171
- Hello.
- You must be...

1701
00:58:19,401 --> 00:58:21,211
- You're pastry chefs.
- That's right.

1702
00:58:22,271 --> 00:58:23,941
- Let's take a look at the breads.
- Shall we?

1703
00:58:23,941 --> 00:58:25,081
- Shall we?
- Gosh.

1704
00:58:25,081 --> 00:58:26,911
(They go into the bakery without hesitation.)

1705
00:58:26,981 --> 00:58:29,751
Gosh. I'm a bread lover.

1706
00:58:30,551 --> 00:58:32,451
- Exactly.
- I love bread.

1707
00:58:32,451 --> 00:58:33,621
That looks good.

1708
00:58:33,951 --> 00:58:35,151
- Mugwort marble bread.
- Yes.

1709
00:58:35,151 --> 00:58:36,461
Why don't we give it a try?

1710
00:58:36,961 --> 00:58:38,791
- Mugwort marble bread.
- He grabbed it right away.

1711
00:58:39,061 --> 00:58:40,861
- Can I buy the melon bread?
- Do you have this?

1712
00:58:40,861 --> 00:58:41,891
(Grabbing)

1713
00:58:42,231 --> 00:58:44,501
- Let's pay for it first.
- Pick one.

1714
00:58:44,501 --> 00:58:45,601
- We should pay.
- Let's pay.

1715
00:58:45,601 --> 00:58:46,901
We'll pay. Choose first.

1716
00:58:47,401 --> 00:58:49,741
- I'll get a scone.
- Do you like scones?

1717
00:58:49,741 --> 00:58:51,071
(They start shopping for bread when they said they were full.)

1718
00:58:52,271 --> 00:58:53,611
It's a walnut cranberry bagel.

1719
00:58:54,071 --> 00:58:55,371
I want an egg tart.

1720
00:58:56,781 --> 00:58:59,011
(Giggling)

1721
00:58:59,081 --> 00:59:00,711
(Amazed)

1722
00:59:00,811 --> 00:59:02,511
- He's so tall.
- I know.

1723
00:59:03,251 --> 00:59:04,451
- He's taller than our hat.
- Yes.

1724
00:59:05,121 --> 00:59:06,921
- I love bagels.
- They're good.

1725
00:59:07,091 --> 00:59:08,621
I've never paid today.

1726
00:59:08,621 --> 00:59:09,961
Are you going to buy these breads?

1727
00:59:09,961 --> 00:59:11,091
Of course, I am.

1728
00:59:11,461 --> 00:59:12,591
It's my turn now.

1729
00:59:12,591 --> 00:59:14,431
There are so many tasty breads.

1730
00:59:14,631 --> 00:59:16,631
- Thank you.
- There are so many.

1731
00:59:17,731 --> 00:59:19,261
I'll pay for them all.

1732
00:59:19,261 --> 00:59:20,801
- Are you really buying them?
- Yes, Jae Seok.

1733
00:59:21,831 --> 00:59:22,941
Is Young Hyun really paying?

1734
00:59:23,841 --> 00:59:25,171
Wait. Whose is this?

1735
00:59:25,171 --> 00:59:26,611
- Mine.
- Right.

1736
00:59:26,611 --> 00:59:28,271
- What about this one?
- That's mine.

1737
00:59:28,271 --> 00:59:29,641
- This one?
- That's mine.

1738
00:59:29,811 --> 00:59:31,011
I bought so much.

1739
00:59:31,011 --> 00:59:33,211
(Jae Seok picked 4 breads.)

1740
00:59:34,151 --> 00:59:35,381
- Thank you, Young Hyun.
- Yes.

1741
00:59:35,481 --> 00:59:37,121
- I'll enjoy them at home.
- Sure.

1742
00:59:38,051 --> 00:59:39,591
- This way.
- Thank you.

1743
00:59:39,851 --> 00:59:41,451
- Let's go now.
- Shall we?

1744
00:59:41,621 --> 00:59:43,591
- Let's go this way first.
- What a great course.

1745
00:59:44,021 --> 00:59:45,661
We bought the bread...

1746
00:59:45,861 --> 00:59:47,061
- from Whenever Guest's workplace.
- Yes.

1747
00:59:47,731 --> 00:59:50,431
This is why they go to work at 5:30am.

1748
00:59:50,431 --> 00:59:52,701
(They follow Whenever Guest deeper into the hotel.)

1749
00:59:52,731 --> 00:59:54,171
This is the staff hallway.

1750
00:59:54,271 --> 00:59:55,701
Is this the staff passage?

1751
00:59:56,231 --> 00:59:57,271
(A staff hallway appears after making many turns.)

1752
00:59:57,271 --> 00:59:59,041
- Gosh. This is...
- Goodness.

1753
00:59:59,041 --> 01:00:01,641
- It's somewhere we can't come in.
- We can't come in here.

1754
01:00:02,311 --> 01:00:04,481
- This is the VIP passage.
- Exactly.

1755
01:00:04,511 --> 01:00:06,381
- This place is really...
- It's fancy.

1756
01:00:07,981 --> 01:00:09,781
There must be so many staff members.

1757
01:00:10,281 --> 01:00:11,551
Gosh. This is it.

1758
01:00:12,181 --> 01:00:13,991
It's a staff lounge.

1759
01:00:13,991 --> 01:00:15,121
(Staff lounge)

1760
01:00:15,151 --> 01:00:17,091
This is the staff lounge?

1761
01:00:17,091 --> 01:00:18,861
Yes. We take a break here.

1762
01:00:18,861 --> 01:00:20,191
(A lounge designated for hotel staff to take some rest)

1763
01:00:20,761 --> 01:00:22,061
Are these soundproof booths?

1764
01:00:22,061 --> 01:00:23,501
Yes. When we make phone calls, you can't hear it.

1765
01:00:23,501 --> 01:00:24,831
- It's for making calls.
- Yes.

1766
01:00:24,901 --> 01:00:26,231
We can't hear it from the outside.

1767
01:00:26,231 --> 01:00:27,431
Wait. You can't really hear it?

1768
01:00:27,631 --> 01:00:29,271
No. We tried a few times.

1769
01:00:29,371 --> 01:00:30,401
Try it.

1770
01:00:30,771 --> 01:00:32,941
- You try it.
- Can you hear me?

1771
01:00:32,941 --> 01:00:34,071
- We can hear you.
- What? I can hear him.

1772
01:00:34,411 --> 01:00:35,441
I can hear you loud and clear.

1773
01:00:35,441 --> 01:00:36,511
What? Wait.

1774
01:00:36,511 --> 01:00:37,711
- We couldn't hear it before.
- What's going on?

1775
01:00:37,711 --> 01:00:39,781
- We aren't that loud.
- You can't talk loudly in there.

1776
01:00:39,781 --> 01:00:41,611
I didn't speak loudly.

1777
01:00:41,751 --> 01:00:43,081
I just said, "Can you hear me?"

1778
01:00:43,581 --> 01:00:44,721
- You said, "I can hear you."
- I can't believe it.

1779
01:00:44,781 --> 01:00:46,051
We weren't supposed to hear it.

1780
01:00:46,821 --> 01:00:48,451
It was so loud and clear.

1781
01:00:48,651 --> 01:00:50,991
- This way?
- Yes. You can sit on both sides.

1782
01:00:51,291 --> 01:00:53,691
Gosh. The rest of us picked one piece of bread each.

1783
01:00:54,361 --> 01:00:56,161
This is pathetic when I'm the oldest one.

1784
01:00:57,031 --> 01:00:59,431
But there were many kinds of bread that I liked.

1785
01:00:59,631 --> 01:01:00,801
(Amazed)

1786
01:01:01,101 --> 01:01:04,341
They've made a cake for us.

1787
01:01:04,341 --> 01:01:05,901
Gosh. That's amazing.

1788
01:01:05,901 --> 01:01:07,571
(Whenever Guests made these breads themselves.)

1789
01:01:07,571 --> 01:01:09,741
It's too precious to eat.

1790
01:01:09,741 --> 01:01:10,881
Gosh. It's so pretty.

1791
01:01:11,181 --> 01:01:12,911
Gosh. It's a mango cake.

1792
01:01:15,011 --> 01:01:16,781
- You shouldn't have taken us...
- Jae Seok.

1793
01:01:16,781 --> 01:01:18,151
to eat bingsu.

1794
01:01:18,151 --> 01:01:19,851
(They cleared 3 bingsus.)

1795
01:01:19,991 --> 01:01:21,251
- They had bingsu.
- And red bean brownie...

1796
01:01:21,251 --> 01:01:22,521
They love bingsu.

1797
01:01:22,991 --> 01:01:25,161
- Let's try the cake.
- Shall we?

1798
01:01:25,991 --> 01:01:27,831
Does anyone have a birthday coming up?

1799
01:01:28,731 --> 01:01:29,961
- A birthday.
- Birthday.

1800
01:01:31,501 --> 01:01:33,431
- My birthday was on the 17th.
- I see.

1801
01:01:33,431 --> 01:01:35,131
Happy birthday to you

1802
01:01:35,271 --> 01:01:36,941
(Celebrating his birthday which was 2 weeks ago...)

1803
01:01:36,941 --> 01:01:38,041
(since they have a cake)

1804
01:01:39,001 --> 01:01:41,271
(Happy)

1805
01:01:41,511 --> 01:01:44,411
(Throwing an unexpected birthday party for Seung Ho)

1806
01:01:44,411 --> 01:01:45,981
(Happy birthday to you)

1807
01:01:45,981 --> 01:01:48,381
- Gosh. Thank you.
- It's in August. That's right.

1808
01:01:49,251 --> 01:01:50,381
- Let's try it.
- Let's try it quickly.

1809
01:01:50,381 --> 01:01:53,251
- I want to try it.
- But it's too precious to cut it.

1810
01:01:54,221 --> 01:01:55,751
- I'll try it now.
- Okay.

1811
01:01:55,751 --> 01:01:57,791
- Please enjoy.
- Share it with Young K.

1812
01:01:57,791 --> 01:01:59,591
- The premium cream...
- Gosh.

1813
01:01:59,591 --> 01:02:00,931
tastes different.

1814
01:02:01,291 --> 01:02:03,631
Gosh. It has so many mango pieces.

1815
01:02:03,731 --> 01:02:04,901
(Satisfied)

1816
01:02:04,901 --> 01:02:06,161
I'm eating like a king today.

1817
01:02:06,401 --> 01:02:07,531
Yes, Seung Ho.

1818
01:02:07,531 --> 01:02:09,101
- We're eating like kings.
- Really.

1819
01:02:09,231 --> 01:02:11,471
Do the three of you...

1820
01:02:11,471 --> 01:02:13,541
play different parts?

1821
01:02:13,541 --> 01:02:14,641
- How does it work?
- How does it work?

1822
01:02:14,641 --> 01:02:17,241
I'm responsible for cakes and buffet.

1823
01:02:17,541 --> 01:02:19,011
- I see.
- You made this, then.

1824
01:02:19,011 --> 01:02:20,251
Yes, I made it.

1825
01:02:20,251 --> 01:02:21,611
- She made it this morning.
- Yes.

1826
01:02:21,611 --> 01:02:23,011
- Did you make it this morning?
- Yes.

1827
01:02:23,011 --> 01:02:24,381
- What time?
- I prepped for it yesterday.

1828
01:02:24,381 --> 01:02:25,421
(It's so good.)

1829
01:02:25,421 --> 01:02:27,691
I made the chocolates over here.

1830
01:02:27,691 --> 01:02:28,751
- These?
- I see.

1831
01:02:29,051 --> 01:02:30,391
These chocolates.

1832
01:02:30,391 --> 01:02:31,691
There are four pieces.

1833
01:02:31,691 --> 01:02:35,691
I'm responsible for the buffet and mousse cakes.

1834
01:02:35,691 --> 01:02:38,361
I made the mille-feuille cake you saw upstairs.

1835
01:02:38,361 --> 01:02:40,031
- The fig mille-feuille.
- Yes.

1836
01:02:40,331 --> 01:02:41,531
- That looked good too.
- By the way,

1837
01:02:41,531 --> 01:02:43,371
are you all the same age?

1838
01:02:43,371 --> 01:02:45,701
Yu Jin and I are the same age.

1839
01:02:45,701 --> 01:02:47,071
Su Bin is one year older than us.

1840
01:02:47,611 --> 01:02:49,411
How long have you been working here?

1841
01:02:49,411 --> 01:02:52,681
I started working in 2021, so this is my 6th year.

1842
01:02:52,681 --> 01:02:53,911
- This is your sixth year.
- That's quite a while.

1843
01:02:53,911 --> 01:02:55,581
What about you two?

1844
01:02:55,581 --> 01:02:57,521
- I started next.
- And I started working.

1845
01:02:57,521 --> 01:02:59,991
- Su Bin is the newest one.
- Yes. I'm just the oldest one.

1846
01:03:02,791 --> 01:03:04,061
You're the oldest one.

1847
01:03:04,061 --> 01:03:05,621
- You're one year older than them.
- Yes.

1848
01:03:07,131 --> 01:03:11,501
(They've walked the same path toward the same dream.)

1849
01:03:14,171 --> 01:03:16,741
(They're more than coworkers now.)

1850
01:03:16,741 --> 01:03:22,371
(They're friends who support one another.)

1851
01:03:22,641 --> 01:03:26,911
How did you become a pastry chef, Ye Won?

1852
01:03:26,911 --> 01:03:28,281
When did you start dreaming of becoming one?

1853
01:03:28,281 --> 01:03:30,021
We all had the same reason.

1854
01:03:30,021 --> 01:03:31,181
(Laughing)

1855
01:03:32,181 --> 01:03:34,951
- There was "Yumeiro Patissiere."
- Okay.

1856
01:03:35,151 --> 01:03:37,221
- It was an animation.
- Yes.

1857
01:03:37,221 --> 01:03:38,321
Do you know it?

1858
01:03:38,321 --> 01:03:39,391
No, not really.

1859
01:03:39,991 --> 01:03:41,631
It's so famous.

1860
01:03:41,631 --> 01:03:42,691
- Is it?
- Yes.

1861
01:03:42,691 --> 01:03:43,701
(Young K knows about the animation.)

1862
01:03:43,701 --> 01:03:47,071
- Do you know it?
- There was a popular challenge...

1863
01:03:47,071 --> 01:03:49,471
where you dance along its soundtrack.

1864
01:03:49,941 --> 01:03:51,841
It's so famous.

1865
01:03:52,001 --> 01:03:53,141
(NCT WISH, THE BOYZ, TWS)

1866
01:03:53,141 --> 01:03:56,111
(It was a super popular challenge in 2021 joined by many idols.)

1867
01:03:56,141 --> 01:04:00,211
(Young K did the challenge too.)

1868
01:04:00,611 --> 01:04:02,051
(Thanks to the challenge, )

1869
01:04:02,051 --> 01:04:04,281
(the soundtrack by IU made it back to the charts.)

1870
01:04:04,351 --> 01:04:06,221
You gave us lots of hints.

1871
01:04:06,721 --> 01:04:08,821
IU sang this song.

1872
01:04:08,821 --> 01:04:09,861
- Yes.
- That's right.

1873
01:04:09,861 --> 01:04:12,221
Come to think of it...

1874
01:04:13,161 --> 01:04:14,391
IU must be so happy.

1875
01:04:15,191 --> 01:04:16,631
(He envies her.)

1876
01:04:17,101 --> 01:04:19,161
- Because she sang the song.
- Right.

1877
01:04:19,361 --> 01:04:21,531
There are animations of our time too.

1878
01:04:21,801 --> 01:04:23,671
Did you dream of becoming a pastry chef after watching it?

1879
01:04:23,671 --> 01:04:24,871
Yes.

1880
01:04:24,871 --> 01:04:27,911
I loved this animation when I was young.

1881
01:04:27,911 --> 01:04:29,011
I watched it over and over again,

1882
01:04:29,011 --> 01:04:31,011
thinking it would be fun to do something like that.

1883
01:04:31,011 --> 01:04:33,211
May I ask what your favorite kind of bread is?

1884
01:04:33,211 --> 01:04:36,051
It's the Hokkaido bread over here.

1885
01:04:36,051 --> 01:04:38,351
- I see.
- It's my favorite.

1886
01:04:38,351 --> 01:04:39,351
Hokkaido?

1887
01:04:39,351 --> 01:04:40,691
- Is this your favorite?
- Yes.

1888
01:04:41,151 --> 01:04:42,291
Okay. Gosh.

1889
01:04:44,221 --> 01:04:46,731
We did eat a lot today.

1890
01:04:47,131 --> 01:04:48,631
But we have to taste it.

1891
01:04:48,631 --> 01:04:50,631
(They have to give it a try as it's her favorite.)

1892
01:04:50,631 --> 01:04:53,231
Sorry. We love bread so much.

1893
01:04:53,231 --> 01:04:54,371
(Filling an already full stomach with cream-filled bread)

1894
01:04:54,371 --> 01:04:56,271
We've been eating so much nonstop.

1895
01:04:56,431 --> 01:04:57,941
(The big eater is fine.)

1896
01:04:57,941 --> 01:04:59,271
What's the cream inside?

1897
01:04:59,401 --> 01:05:01,841
- It's condensed milk cream.
- It's condensed milk.

1898
01:05:01,841 --> 01:05:03,811
- The bread itself is so soft.
- Gosh. This one.

1899
01:05:04,311 --> 01:05:06,851
- It must be good with coffee.
- It's perfect with an Americano.

1900
01:05:06,851 --> 01:05:07,881
- Yes.
- An Americano.

1901
01:05:08,281 --> 01:05:11,021
Which bread do you like the most, Ye Won?

1902
01:05:11,021 --> 01:05:12,281
I love this one.

1903
01:05:12,281 --> 01:05:13,521
- This one?
- Yes.

1904
01:05:14,291 --> 01:05:15,521
I'm sorry.

1905
01:05:17,421 --> 01:05:18,461
It's unfortunate.

1906
01:05:18,461 --> 01:05:21,261
(She likes a different one.)

1907
01:05:22,031 --> 01:05:24,331
We should try it a little.

1908
01:05:24,561 --> 01:05:26,131
- She likes this one.
- Now, Young Hyun.

1909
01:05:26,131 --> 01:05:27,601
- Yes.
- Seung Ho.

1910
01:05:27,601 --> 01:05:28,701
Yes.

1911
01:05:28,701 --> 01:05:30,041
Let's just try a little.

1912
01:05:32,571 --> 01:05:34,441
- We have to cut it well.
- They're just holding the forks.

1913
01:05:36,511 --> 01:05:38,581
- We did eat a lot.
- I can't do it, Jae Seok.

1914
01:05:38,581 --> 01:05:39,581
It's...

1915
01:05:40,781 --> 01:05:43,011
- He's full.
- I'm really full.

1916
01:05:43,011 --> 01:05:44,951
(His stomach is at capacity.)

1917
01:05:45,081 --> 01:05:47,091
This one is good too. It's tasty.

1918
01:05:47,821 --> 01:05:50,561
Your mother sent us the letter.

1919
01:05:50,561 --> 01:05:51,561
That's right.

1920
01:05:51,561 --> 01:05:53,191
My mom has never missed an episode...

1921
01:05:53,191 --> 01:05:55,091
since Season One of this show.

1922
01:05:55,091 --> 01:05:56,131
- I see.
- Yes.

1923
01:05:56,131 --> 01:05:57,261
She always told me...

1924
01:05:57,261 --> 01:05:59,001
to send a letter.

1925
01:05:59,001 --> 01:06:00,531
- She always said that.
- Gosh.

1926
01:06:00,531 --> 01:06:02,831
But I always said I was too shy to do it.

1927
01:06:02,831 --> 01:06:04,871
And suddenly Mom messaged me,

1928
01:06:04,871 --> 01:06:07,511
saying "I sent the letter."

1929
01:06:08,511 --> 01:06:10,441
- She wrote lots of comments...
- Really?

1930
01:06:10,441 --> 01:06:12,281
on YouTube before.

1931
01:06:12,281 --> 01:06:13,611
Did she leave many comments?

1932
01:06:13,611 --> 01:06:15,711
- Has she been active in this field?
- Yes.

1933
01:06:15,711 --> 01:06:18,181
- On Choi Hwa Jeong's channel, - Yes.

1934
01:06:18,181 --> 01:06:19,381
she left a comment...

1935
01:06:19,381 --> 01:06:21,291
with the cake I made on Christmas.

1936
01:06:21,291 --> 01:06:23,691
The comment said, "My daughter made this."

1937
01:06:24,721 --> 01:06:27,391
(She couldn't help but brag about her daughter.)

1938
01:06:27,391 --> 01:06:29,261
It wasn't just on our channel.

1939
01:06:29,261 --> 01:06:30,501
She left them on all channels.

1940
01:06:30,501 --> 01:06:32,461
(Her 1st fan has been active in many areas.)

1941
01:06:32,461 --> 01:06:33,731
She's cute.

1942
01:06:34,071 --> 01:06:35,071
Good.

1943
01:06:35,071 --> 01:06:37,641
Anyway, since we're here,

1944
01:06:37,641 --> 01:06:39,571
we should go for it and win presents.

1945
01:06:39,571 --> 01:06:40,711
- Yes.
- Gosh.

1946
01:06:41,371 --> 01:06:43,611
- Ye Won.
- Crack the cookie for Round One.

1947
01:06:43,611 --> 01:06:45,311
- Should I do it?
- Crack it open.

1948
01:06:45,311 --> 01:06:48,381
"The mark of the chef's hat is the trace of hard work."

1949
01:06:48,381 --> 01:06:49,811
"I want to cover it nicely."

1950
01:06:49,811 --> 01:06:52,081
"Three Polo Ralph Lauren ball caps."

1951
01:06:52,081 --> 01:06:53,691
(Round 1 present: 3 Polo ball caps)

1952
01:06:53,691 --> 01:06:55,591
- Ball caps.
- From Ralph Lauren.

1953
01:06:56,051 --> 01:06:57,591
- Is each of them different?
- Yes.

1954
01:06:57,591 --> 01:06:59,091
- We wear caps all the time.
- Look at the colors.

1955
01:07:00,231 --> 01:07:01,661
- They're pretty.
- I know.

1956
01:07:01,661 --> 01:07:03,031
The logos are different.

1957
01:07:03,131 --> 01:07:04,531
(Land It on the Chef’s Hat!)

1958
01:07:04,531 --> 01:07:06,201
(Bound a table-tennis ball...)

1959
01:07:06,201 --> 01:07:08,071
(and put it in the chef's hat on a head.)

1960
01:07:08,171 --> 01:07:10,801
(But there are only 7 table-tennis balls.)

1961
01:07:10,801 --> 01:07:11,871
We did it before.

1962
01:07:12,241 --> 01:07:13,711
We played it with Choo Sung Hoon.

1963
01:07:13,711 --> 01:07:15,611
- It's like that one.
- We put it in there.

1964
01:07:16,441 --> 01:07:18,181
It's something like that.

1965
01:07:18,341 --> 01:07:21,381
The next person can only go if the previous one succeeds.

1966
01:07:21,381 --> 01:07:22,581
Gosh. This is...

1967
01:07:22,581 --> 01:07:23,681
So...

1968
01:07:24,181 --> 01:07:25,721
- I see.
- If one fails, it's over.

1969
01:07:25,721 --> 01:07:26,721
This one is hard.

1970
01:07:26,721 --> 01:07:28,391
We have to pull it off at once.

1971
01:07:28,391 --> 01:07:29,391
(They all have to succeed with 7 balls.)

1972
01:07:29,391 --> 01:07:30,961
- Place it well on the hat.
- Isn't it too hard?

1973
01:07:30,961 --> 01:07:32,091
- It faces that way, right?
- I see.

1974
01:07:32,161 --> 01:07:33,431
There's no front and back to this hat.

1975
01:07:33,431 --> 01:07:34,631
- Here.
- Yes.

1976
01:07:34,631 --> 01:07:35,631
(Wearing the combat hat)

1977
01:07:35,631 --> 01:07:38,431
- Let me see. I'll look.
- Round 1 is 1 thing, but...

1978
01:07:38,431 --> 01:07:39,461
(Checking their looks amiably)

1979
01:07:39,461 --> 01:07:40,901
I don't know if we can pull through Round Three.

1980
01:07:43,501 --> 01:07:44,541
It won't be easy.

1981
01:07:44,541 --> 01:07:47,471
(Struggling alone)

1982
01:07:47,471 --> 01:07:48,971
The hat doesn't fit.

1983
